{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence","id":975837,"title":"Shell metis Gift vs vampiric Presence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-24T22:32:21-07:00","id":975837,"title":"Shell metis Gift vs vampiric Presence","content":"I'm wondering what people think of Presence being able to bypass the Shell Gift? Dominate is obviously direct mind control and would be blocked but what about emotion manipulation like Presence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T22:39:46-07:00","id":975839,"title":"","content":"I would say yes. It says that it protects them from all mind altering magic and Presence does alter the mind. In fact, it even mentions that it is an emotional barrier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T05:07:35-07:00","id":975915,"title":"","content":"Indeed, it should protect you also from the powers of animalism and the thaumaturgy paths that deals with the mind.<br /> Problem is you can't use rage while using Shell, so it is great to resist mind effects, but makes you vulnerable in fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T08:23:43-07:00","id":975950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=975915#post975915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, it should protect you also from the powers of animalism and the thaumaturgy paths that deals with the mind.<br /> Problem is you can't use rage while using Shell, so it is great to resist mind effects, but makes you vulnerable in fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some Gifts or circumstances can mollify that drawback in various ways. For instance, using Create Element to set the vampire on fire or some other use of a Gift that requires Gnosis to function, such as Totem Gift (unless you have Chaos Mechanics, you wouldn't be able to use Rage anyway), Out of combat situations, that restriction also tends to matter less, especially if infiltrating an area or already using Bury the Wolf (which also prevents the use of Rage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T11:55:50-07:00","id":997804,"title":"","content":"Depends on how powerful the Vamp is. If the Vampire has mind-altering powers and/or rituals of Level 6+ (in case of some Thau powers, rituals and combo disciplines lower since they are specifically designed against Hardened defence), she burns through the defenses. Even Iron Will can be brought down. But that is not the average Vampire. Against average Vampires mostly Shell will work, not against all, but many. Against true Elders (and some childes of Elders, Baba Yagas childe developed his first Level 6 power within ten years of becoming undead) with high developed disciplines, no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T12:35:52-07:00","id":997828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=997804#post997804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how powerful the Vamp is. If the Vampire has mind-altering powers and/or rituals of Level 6+ (in case of some Thau powers, rituals and combo disciplines lower since they are specifically designed against Hardened defence), she burns through the defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf doesn't work on these assumptions. In particular, it doesn't care about magical 6+ dots in whatever bullshit is around. The Gift no-sells anything that's not a plot device; get over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:48:32-07:00","id":997869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=997828#post997828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf doesn't work on these assumptions. In particular, it doesn't care about magical 6+ dots in whatever bullshit is around. The Gift no-sells anything that's not a plot device; get over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha. Snark aside, I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> on this. Unless it is important to the plot that Shell not work, it should work exactly as intended, even against elder powers.<br /> <br /> With the example of Baba Yaga, plot would most likely said it fails. But it is an important distinction that it is failing due to plot and not some Vampire-Elders-overpower-everything rule.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:53:57-07:00","id":997931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=975915#post975915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is you can't use rage while using Shell, so it is great to resist mind effects, but makes you vulnerable in fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I doubt many vamps know that little tidbit, though, and if you are being actively attacked, the needs of combat often takes precedence over applications of Presence.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T05:47:22-07:00","id":998193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=997828#post997828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf doesn't work on these assumptions. In particular, it doesn't care about magical 6+ dots in whatever bullshit is around. The Gift no-sells anything that's not a plot device; get over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi Sour Ops Specialist!<br /> <br /> I do not have to get over anything, I won 5 \u20ac because I predicted you answering within 1 hour of my post and the rough direction of it correctly. That aside: Chummer, not only did I read some more of WtA in the meantime since I last posted here, I had a nice talk with a Storyteller friend of mine, He has nearly 2 decades experience on gamemstering WtA, his favourite WoD system, VtM and MtA. When I told and showed him some posts of you, esp the ones about what Gnosis can do, he simply laughed and now I quote him: &quot;The next time you discuss something with that guy, simply say yes, do not rob him of his illusions or tell him what I tell you now. I am a longtime WtA gamemaster, talked with other GMs and what this SOS guy writes is 60% wrong rule interpretation, 30% assumptions going into wank territory and 10% correct. Basically he bends the system as he needs it. No matter if you quote the rules to him, he will come with another outrageous rule interpretation. I know that you know yourself that it is useless to discuss much with such guys.&quot; And he is correct on that one!<br /> I was able to make a bet with a collegue. While I was not sure that you would answer before the deadline we set, I am proud that I correctly judged that you would outright deny any rules you dislike and inflate the Gift well outside the rules and intent.<br /> <br /> So stay happy with the way you play WtA, but why you simply do not lay the rulebooks aside (you do not need them anyway with your playstyle) and just sing Pippi Longstocking\u00b4s song as the guideline of how you play WtA, that is your secret.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T06:08:46-07:00","id":998198,"title":"","content":"It's a role-playing game. <i>All</i> the splat vs splat discussion is wank on some level. There are no absolute right answers here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T06:31:11-07:00","id":998201,"title":"","content":"It has been said and done enough times already:<br /> Splat X wins if their rules take precedence. Crossover works only if you take liberties and tinker with the rules.<br /> And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7492_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7492\" data-vbnamecard=\"7492\">G\u00fcnther</a> posts like this may cause people to think you're a troll.<br /> I think it is bad form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T09:55:03-07:00","id":998282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=998201#post998201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been said and done enough times already:<br /> Splat X wins if their rules take precedence. Crossover works only if you take liberties and tinker with the rules.<br /> And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7492_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7492\" data-vbnamecard=\"7492\">G\u00fcnther</a> posts like this may cause people to think you're a troll.<br /> I think it is bad form.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=997804#post997804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even Iron Will can be brought down. But that is not the average Vampire. Against average Vampires mostly Shell will work, not against all, but many. Against true Elders (and some childes of Elders, Baba Yagas childe developed his first Level 6 power within ten years of becoming undead) with high developed disciplines, no.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the rules crunch side of things, comparing a Gift that specifically says it protects against certain powers without caveat to a Merit that says it fails against certain levels isn't a good example. Shell is much better than Iron Will in general, as it should be.<br /> <br /> And it should certainly work against Sergei Voshkov. Why wouldn't it? (this is an honest question from my end)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 11-04-2016, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T10:11:35-07:00","id":998287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=998193#post998193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a nice talk with a Storyteller friend of mine, He has nearly 2 decades experience on gamemstering WtA, his favourite WoD system, VtM and MtA. When I told and showed him some posts of you, esp the ones about what Gnosis can do, he simply laughed and now I quote him: &quot;The next time you discuss something with that guy, simply say yes, do not rob him of his illusions or tell him what I tell you now. I am a longtime WtA gamemaster, talked with other GMs and what this SOS guy writes is 60% wrong rule interpretation, 30% assumptions going into wank territory and 10% correct. Basically he bends the system as he needs it. No matter if you quote the rules to him, he will come with another outrageous rule interpretation. I know that you know yourself that it is useless to discuss much with such guys.&quot; And he is correct on that one!</div> </div> </div> </div>So... Saur is wrong because you talked to a dude and <i>that </i>guy said Saur is wrong? Huh.<br /> <br /> There is a logical fallacy called a 'false appeal to authority,' but this feels like a 'false appeal to irrelevant outsider.' Being told you are wrong on the internet by some random guy is one thing, but being told you are wrong on the internet by some random guy's friend? That's some next level shit right there.<br /> <br /> Someone remind me to ask my brother's dog about his opinion on mutant werewolves and how they interact with elder-level disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T11:22:59-07:00","id":998328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=998201#post998201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has been said and done enough times already:<br /> Splat X wins if their rules take precedence. Crossover works only if you take liberties and tinker with the rules.<br /> And <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7492_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7492\" data-vbnamecard=\"7492\">G\u00fcnther</a> posts like this may cause people to think you're a troll.<br /> I think it is bad form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi!<br /> <br /> I dislike this &quot;trolling&quot; myself, but I am simply fed up with the way certain factions among the forum users just wank their faction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7492-g\u00fcnther","name":"G\u00fcnther","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:10:47-07:00","id":998363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=998328#post998328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hi!<br /> <br /> I dislike this &amp;quot;trolling&amp;quot; myself, but I am simply fed up with the way certain factions among the forum users just wank their faction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then let me advice you that your current path reminds me of a rote called \u201cFanning Passion's Flames\u201c.<br /> <br /> I am also [...] my faction. It is natural human behavior. But putting oil in the fire is not helpful.<br /> If you are displeased with someone or something it should not be impossible to make your point clear without resorting to flames.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T12:23:26-07:00","id":998372,"title":"","content":"All in all, this trolling seems like kind of a pointless reason to have revived this thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T13:13:58-07:00","id":998407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>G\u00fcnther</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/975837-shell-metis-gift-vs-vampiric-presence?p=998193#post998193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Sour Ops Specialist!<br /> <br /> I do not have to get over anything, I won 5 \u20ac because I predicted you answering within 1 hour of my post and the rough direction of it correctly. That aside: Chummer, not only did I read some more of WtA in the meantime since I last posted here, I had a nice talk with a Storyteller friend of mine, He has nearly 2 decades experience on gamemstering WtA, his favourite WoD system, VtM and MtA. When I told and showed him some posts of you, esp the ones about what Gnosis can do, he simply laughed and now I quote him: &amp;quot;The next time you discuss something with that guy, simply say yes, do not rob him of his illusions or tell him what I tell you now. I am a longtime WtA gamemaster, talked with other GMs and what this SOS guy writes is 60% wrong rule interpretation, 30% assumptions going into wank territory and 10% correct. Basically he bends the system as he needs it. No matter if you quote the rules to him, he will come with another outrageous rule interpretation. I know that you know yourself that it is useless to discuss much with such guys.&amp;quot; And he is correct on that one!<br /> I was able to make a bet with a collegue. While I was not sure that you would answer before the deadline we set, I am proud that I correctly judged that you would outright deny any rules you dislike and inflate the Gift well outside the rules and intent.<br /> <br /> So stay happy with the way you play WtA, but why you simply do not lay the rulebooks aside (you do not need them anyway with your playstyle) and just sing Pippi Longstocking\u00b4s song as the guideline of how you play WtA, that is your secret.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">This post serves no purpose but to insult Saur Ops Specialist, and is a flagrant violation of rule 1 of thes forums. Since you are a relatively new member and this is a first offense, I'm just going to give you a warning. But so you know, posts like this will earn you suspensions in the future, and a repeated pattern of rules violations could result in a permanent ban.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:27:53-08:00","id":1001061,"title":"","content":"Well...this post certainly went much further than I thought it would. Should check in more often. Thanks all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1546-great-cthulhu","name":"Great Cthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1546_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}